  "note": "Step 7 speculative fixture (derivation A): every expect is derived by hand from the 60-wire topology (ER-34 applied) and the p.24-25 rule, not printed; the printed end-state claim (light 1 after twelve steps) is in V-EXP14. Topology: relay n coil runs nF-coil-nE-indicator lamp-nC, the 1C..6C chain on minus, so each indicator lamp lights with its coil. Relay 6 latches from 6+ through 6H-6G = 6F; relay k (k = 5..1) latches through kH = (k+1)G, which is plus only while relay k+1 holds, so the chain holds from the top. Pushbutton j (arms 1Y..6Y on plus) feeds jX = jS; with slide switch j LEFT, jS-jR reaches (7-j)com; pushbutton 1 reaches 6com = 6F directly, and pushbutton j > 1 reaches (8-j)L, whose N.O. (8-j)K is the feed (7-j)F, so relay 7-j is called only while relay 8-j is in. Sneak paths checked: the 1T..6T chain joins only RIGHT-thrown switch arms and open pushbutton N.O. contacts; the 2N..6N chain joins only com junctions of released relays and their R contacts; neither reaches a coil feed or minus. Script choices, not printed: three wrong-order steps (pushbutton 1 before slide switch 1; slide switch 2 and pushbutton 2 before steps 1-2; slide switch 3 and pushbutton 3 after steps 1-2), each checked while the button is held, then undone by returning the slide switch RIGHT; one expect after each relay-calling push, with steps 9-11 merged; 200 ms advances before each expect to let lamp filaments settle.",
